{"id": "sevt_0147598fYUoUQduowhXALQFu", "content": [{"text": "**Evidence**\n- The cart deploy `0c1986c` went out at 14:16:45. Cart p99 went from about 76 ms at 14:15 to 3,956 ms at 14:16, and stayed at 3.9\u20135.9k ms through 14:59. The jump comes within about a minute of the deploy, and the 14:16 sample may already include post-deploy traffic.\n- The checkout deploy `21acf62` at 14:15:30 is a possible confounder. I did not read its diff or check checkout metrics. Cart's own deploy lines up more tightly with the spike.\n- The diff to `cart/pricing.py` replaces one batched `sku_id IN (...)` query with one `SELECT ... WHERE sku_id = ?` per cart line. That is the N+1 pattern the runbook lists first.\n- The log shows the same change. Before the deploy, cart issues single `sku_id IN (?)` queries taking about 5\u201316 ms. After it, there are 4,409 per-row `sku_id = ?` queries. I did not check per-request query counts or durations after the deploy.\n\n**Root cause:** `0c1986c` \u2014 it replaced the single batched `sku_prices` query in `price_cart` with one query per cart line (N+1), so cart latency grows with cart size and p99 rose from about 76 ms to about 4 s. Reverting it, or restoring the batched `IN` query, should fix it.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:42:32.904311Z", "type": "agent.message"}
